## Project Overview

This project implements a **production-grade hybrid AWS network** that mirrors how large enterprises actually connect their on-premises data centers to AWS. It combines three of the most important AWS networking patterns into a single working architecture:

**1. Multi-VPC segmentation** — Three separate VPCs (Web, App, DB) representing a classic 3-tier application architecture, each with its own security boundary.

**2. Transit Gateway route isolation** — Strict routing rules enforced at the network layer, not the security group layer. Traffic that has no route is silently dropped before it even reaches its destination.

**3. Hybrid connectivity via Site-to-Site VPN** — A simulated on-premises environment connected to AWS through an IPSec VPN tunnel using libreswan, replicating how a real corporate data center connects to the cloud.

This is not a beginner project. It reflects the architecture used by financial institutions, healthcare organizations, and large enterprises running hybrid cloud workloads.

