## Cost Analysis

| Resource | Hourly Rate | 4-hour Cost |
|---|---|---|
| NAT Gateway | $0.045/hr + $0.045/GB | ~$0.18 |
| Site-to-Site VPN | $0.05/hr | ~$0.20 |
| Transit Gateway | $0.05/hr + $0.02/GB data | ~$0.20 |
| EC2 t2.micro x4 | Free tier | $0.00 |
| VPC Endpoints x6 | $0.01/hr each | ~$0.24 |
| Data transfer | $0.01-0.09/GB | ~$0.05 |
| **Total** | | **~$0.87** |

If left running 24 hours: ~$5-6. Always clean up same day.

Most expensive resources: NAT Gateway ($1.08/day), VPN Connection ($1.20/day), Transit Gateway ($1.20/day).

---

## Cleanup Order

```
1.  Terminate all 4 EC2 instances — wait for Terminated state
2.  Delete Site-to-Site VPN Connection — wait for Deleted state
3.  Delete Customer Gateway
4.  Delete NAT Gateway — wait for Deleted state
5.  Release Elastic IP
6.  Delete all TGW Attachments — wait for Deleted state
7.  Delete all 4 TGW Route Tables
8.  Delete Transit Gateway — wait for Deleted state
9.  Detach and delete all 3 Internet Gateways
10. Delete all 6 VPC Endpoints — wait for Deleted state
11. Delete any remaining ENIs in subnets
12. Delete all 6 custom Route Tables
13. Delete all 6 Subnets
14. Delete all Security Groups (skip default SGs)
15. Delete IAM Role EC2-SSM-Role
16. Delete all 4 VPCs (skip Default VPC)
```

